\p
\v 1 \add Finally\add* when¦231518 the¦231523 13th of¦231523 March arrived, it¦231528 was time for everyone to do what the¦231531 letters from the¦231533 king¦231533 said that he had decreed for them to¦231535 do¦231535. The¦231539 enemies¦231539 of¦231539 the¦231540 Jews had¦231538 expected to¦231541 destroy the \add @Jews¦231542\add* on that day but¦231543 just the opposite¦231543 happened—instead, it¦231543 was¦231543 the¦231547 Jews who¦231549 destroyed their enemies.
\v 2 Throughout the empire, the Jews joined together in¦231553 their¦231571 cities¦231553 to¦231559 defend themselves against those¦231561 who¦231561 wanted¦231561 to harm¦231562 them. No one was able to fight back against them¦231567 because¦231568 everyone \add else\add* in the empire had¦231570 become afraid of¦231574 them.
\v 3 All¦231578 the¦231580 leaders¦231580 in each province¦231581, the¦231582 royal officials¦231580, the¦231583 governors¦231583, and¦231584 everyone who worked¦231585 for¦231587 the¦231587 king¦231587 helped the¦231591 Jews¦231591 because¦231592 they had¦231594 become afraid of¦231597 Mordekai¦231597
