\v 18 But¦231842 the¦231842 Jews in¦231846 Shushan¦231846 had gathered¦231847 together \add and fought their enemies\add* on both the 13th and¦231851 the 14th, so¦231854 they¦231854 stopped on the 15th and¦231858 made¦231858 it¦231859 a¦231860 day¦231860 of¦231860 feasting¦231861 and¦231862 celebration.
\v 19 So¦231866 that's why the¦231867 Jews¦231867 who¦231870 live¦231870 in¦231871 the rural¦231872 villages observe¦231873 this holiday on the¦231878 14th \add rather than the 15th\add*. They celebrate with feasting¦231881 and by giving gifts to each¦231886 other.
\s1 The celebration named ‘Purim’
