\p
\v 20 Now Mordekai¦231891 recorded¦231890 everything that had happened and¦231896 sent¦231896 letters¦231897 to¦231898 all¦231900 the Jews throughout the empire, in¦231904 both the¦231909 near¦231909 provinces¦231906 and¦231910 the¦231910 far¦231910 away ones.
\v 21 That decree established an annual holiday on¦231913 the¦231920 14th and¦231922 15th of¦231923 March every¦231928 year,\f + \fr 9:21 \ft The OET-RV gives an approximate time of the year in our calendars, but the Jewish calendar is largely a lunar calendar so the dates of the feast in our calendars moves around a little. In 2024 for example, ‘Purim’ begins on the evening of March 23 in Yisrael/Israel and concludes at sundown on March 24.\f*
\v 22 because those were the days¦231933 when¦231934 the¦231938 Jews no longer \add had to oppose\add* their¦231939 enemies¦231939 and¦231940 that was the¦231940 month¦231940 when¦231941 \add &their\add* sorrow¦231944 and¦231946 mourning¦231946 had changed¦231942 into¦231947 a¦231947 good¦231948 day¦231947. \add Now\add* they were instructed to make¦231949 them¦231950 days¦231951 of¦231951 feasting¦231952 and¦231953 happiness, and¦231954 sending¦231954 of¦231954 gifts¦231958—to each¦231956 other but also¦231958 to¦231959 the needy.
